      "summary": "Researchers at the University of Stuttgart created circular Rydberg atoms, a specialized atomic state where the electron orbits in a wide, stable ring, and set new records for how long, how large, and how stable these atoms can be, keeping one intact for 11 milliseconds. That matters because circular Rydberg atoms are considered promising building blocks for future quantum computers and simulators, and longer-lived…",
